Both are byte for byte. From this directory,

  find src/kernel spec -type f | sort | xargs shasum -a 256 | shasum -a 256

is 3eb08e585c23c45f82ac54cd844ebfdb44e01e8cdceb31a38a6deb9bc3ceab56, and
`diff -r` against a clone at the commit above reports nothing.

Why src/kernel/ rather than src/: his registry resolves
`../../../spec/registry/timers.json` from its own file. Mirroring his tree
keeps that path true from src/ and from dist/ alike, so nothing had to be
edited. Everything under src/kernel/ and spec/ is his; src/index.ts,
package.json, tsconfig.json and this file are ours.

Local changes to his files: none.

Toolchain differences, absorbed by tsconfig.json rather than by edits:
  - his `.ts` import specifiers stay as written; rewriteRelativeImportExtensions
    (TypeScript 5.7+) emits `.js` in dist for our Node16 resolution
  - his four extra checks are on: exactOptionalPropertyTypes,
    noImplicitOverride, verbatimModuleSyntax, erasableSyntaxOnly
  - his tests run as his: `node --test` with type stripping, on node:test and
    node:assert/strict. Node 22.6 or newer.
  - eslint and Prettier skip src/kernel/ and spec/ (root eslint.config.mjs
    and .prettierignore say why)

